WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.471
Because of the explosive popularity of the
Marvel Cinematic Universe, people are more

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:07.560
aware than ever of the weirder characters
from the comic canon.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.130
However, there are a few heroes that will
likely remain on the bench no matter how big

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:15.240
the MCU gets: heroes like Moon Knight.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.380
Depending on who's writing him, he's either
a Batman knockoff or a killer who talks to

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.859
a moon god — when he's not already busy
talking to his multiple personalities.

00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:28.130
Despite being so strange, Moon Knight still
has a cult following, and his fans have clamored

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.130
for years to see him appear on the silver
screen alongside Captain America and the gang.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:38.450
But, despite the fan love, it's a pretty safe
bet that Marvel won't make a Moon Knight movie.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.990
Here’s why...

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.430
Risky religion

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:46.110
When it comes to religion, the Marvel Cinematic
Universe has treaded pretty lightly, outside

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.290
of Captain America’s take on having a bunch
of Norse gods pop up.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:53.320
"There’s only one god ma'am, and I’m pretty
sure he doesn’t dress like that."

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.190
But with Moon Knight, it's impossible to separate
the man and his religion, such as it is.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.570
He draws his powers from the Egyptian moon
god Khonshu, so pretty much any version of

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:07.220
his superhero story would mean introducing
a whole new buncha gods to the MCU.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.450
We already have Asgardians.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.860
Go any deeper, and this world gets a whole
lot more confusing.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:17.370
So, as the story goes, Moon Knight is the
moon god’s chosen one, and becomes a vigilante

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:21.540
to do Khonshu's bidding, which sometimes actually
includes murdering the bad guys.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.600
In case you were wondering, none of this would
really translate to Marvel's cinematic universe

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.600
too well.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.490
Unless it’s handled perfectly, it’s easy
for Moon Knight to come across as little more

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.690
than a murderous, crazy cult-member.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.240
Think less Daredevil, more Zodiac Killer.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.090
That's not gonna sell too many action figures.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.570
Redundant

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.240
One key area where Marvel has been successful
is making its various onscreen characters

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.350
seem distinct.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.840
It takes a mix of great casting and making
the right story decisions, and for the most

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.470
part, Marvel is killing it.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.990
Robert Downey Jr. set the bar pretty high
with Tony Stark, and they were careful enough

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:01.090
with Doctor Strange to make sure he didn’t
just hit the same rich, white guy hero beats.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:05.340
But when it comes to Moon Knight, he falls
into a whole lot of Batman's territory — and

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.530
in case you haven't noticed, Batman's got
a lot of territory.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:14.170
Let's see: rich guy, a mask-wearing vigilante
by night, lives in a mansion built over a

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:19.050
cave, is assisted by a faithful butler, and
uses themed weaponry to take out bad guys.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.050
Sound familiar?

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.410
Yes, Moon Knight is obviously more than just
that and has several differences when more

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.050
closely compared to Batman.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:29.280
But he checks a whole lot of the same boxes
as the Dark Knight.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.010
For the average movie-going audience, it’d
probably be a few boxes too many.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:36.590
Now, while we're on the subject of being like
Batman...

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.150
Too gimmicky

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.930
Batman uses a whole lot of gear and gimmicks.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.190
But imagine if all those Bat-arangs were now,
umm, moon-arangs?

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.850
Is it getting cheesy yet?

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:50.410
Viewers have had decades to get used to Batman's
brand of Bat-themed justice, but it might

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:54.160
be hard to spring an entire moon-gear line-up
on them at once.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.080
Heroes typically have a signature weapon that
makes them stand out — think Iron Man’s

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.960
armor, or Captain America’s shield.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.990
But Moon Knight doesn’t really have that.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:06.290
One look at the guy in action and all audiences
can really tell is that he's kind of all over

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.819
the place.

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:09.069
Mental health

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:15.099
Mental illness is a delicate subject in general,
and it gets even dicier when it comes to superheroes.

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:19.489
After all, anyone who puts on spandex and
spends their nights punching people must have

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:21.260
more than a few screws loose, right?

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.540
"Oh no, I’m just standing around, ya know.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:24.040
Huh!

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.040
No I’m not!

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:25.540
Ahh!"

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:30.680
However, Moon Knight is established as literally
not sane in the comics on multiple occasions.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.620
That could be tough to bring to life on the
big screen in a respectful way.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.300
A major part of Moon Knight's madness is his
multiple personalities.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:44.240
The roster ranges from taxi driver Jake Lockley,
mercenary Marc Spector, and even other superheroes

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.760
like Spider-Man, Wolverine, and Captain America.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:51.040
At times, they all interact in Moon Knight’s
head, which would not be easy to portray in

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.150
live action.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:56.680
Unfortunately, if moviegoers aren't ready
for a super-violent religious zealot for a

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.150
hero, they're definitely not ready for an
outright unhinged one.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.050
That outfit

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:06.099
Let's be honest: Moon Knight's costume would
be one of the toughest to make look cool on

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:07.099
the big screen.

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:10.940
It's true that most superhero costumes look
at least a little goofy in their original

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:11.940
comics.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.819
But the tried and true ways of fixing that
in a movie wouldn’t work here.

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:18.069
The typical move is to make it leather, and
make it darker.

00:04:18.069 --> 00:04:23.309
For instance, Scarlet Witch's bright red spandex
became a maroon jacket and black pants, while

00:04:23.309 --> 00:04:27.479
Hawkeye's purple get-up morphed into a nearly
all-black outfit on film.

00:04:27.479 --> 00:04:29.349
But Moon Knight’s costume is white.

00:04:29.349 --> 00:04:30.669
Like, all white.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:34.960
If they made it darker, it wouldn’t be Moon
Knight, and after a few bloody fights, that

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.669
all-white costume would start to look pretty
rough.

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:41.610
Realistically, he’d spend most of the movie
looking like a super-hobo once the action

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.159
started.

00:04:43.159 --> 00:04:44.719
Better on TV

00:04:44.719 --> 00:04:49.319
It's been rumored for the better part of a
decade that a Moon Knight TV show could happen.

00:04:49.319 --> 00:04:53.219
Though we’d love to see him get a shot at
big screen glory, it’s obvious the character

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:55.330
would be better served on the boob tube.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:59.460
Having an entire season to develop his character
— all of them— would allow audiences to

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.469
digest the complexities of all his different
personas.

00:05:02.469 --> 00:05:07.639
Put simply, it’d take a TV season to provide
the breathing room for the villains, the supporting

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:11.319
cast, and world-building necessary to make
Moon Knight work.

00:05:11.319 --> 00:05:15.349
His character seems tailor-made for Netflix,
which already features Marvel anti-heroes

00:05:15.349 --> 00:05:17.729
tortured by guilt, loss, and trauma.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:22.309
Then, if Moon Knight doesn't end up fitting
in with Jessica Jones and Luke Cage at first,

00:05:22.309 --> 00:05:25.139
he can just keep swapping personalities until
he does.

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:26.139
Problem solved!

00:05:26.139 --> 00:05:27.139
Thanks for watching!

00:05:27.139 --> 00:05:29.680
